<!--
    M3 Filled Tonal IconButton background — circular tonal surface.

    M3 specifies:
      Filled Tonal IconButton
        container = secondaryContainer (light: #E8DEF8, dark: #4A4458)
        icon       = onSecondaryContainer

    The pin window is an overlay on top of arbitrary underlying apps
    (the home screen, another app, a coloured wallpaper, …) so we
    can't read the Activity's theme attributes from a drawable XML.
    Instead we hard-code the dark-theme surfaceContainerHighest value
    with a translucent alpha — this keeps the close button readable
    on light backgrounds (where solid black would be jarring) AND on
    dark backgrounds (where the tonal surface still has contrast).

    The button size is fixed at 40dp (M3 IconButton's standard hit
    area). The visible circle is the full 40dp — M3's IconButton has
    no padding between hit-area and visual container, unlike
    "standard" IconButton which uses 8dp padding.
-->
<shape xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:shape="oval">
    <solid android:color="#CC424750" />
    <size
        android:width="40dp"
        android:height="40dp" />
</shape>